d y were also widely praised for  their online system with the player  search system offering new ways to meet  battle and trade with others more easily  in 2014 gba games ruby and sapphire were  remade for the 3ds the games saw quite a  drastic overhaul with many modern  elements incorporated from later games  such as 3d mega evolutions the new fairy  type super training pokemon me and over  100 tms in comparison to the 50 the game  originally shipped with the game had new  characters added and new mechanics like  the pokenav plus to take advantage of  the 3ds's second screen omega ruby and  alpha sapphire were huge upgrades to the  original games x and y took us to france  so sun and moon took us to the  hawaii-inspired alola region some  pokemon had alolan forms and therefore  looked different other common terms were  renamed for the new location gyms became  island trials a number of puzzles and  battles ending in a battle with the  island kahuna and the battle tower was  the battle tree z moves were introduced  as a strong pokemon move that's only  able to be used once per battle and in  classic pokemon style enhanced versions  of the generation 7 games followed  shortly after with ultra sun and ultra  moon introducing new alolan forms of  pokemon as well as some story changes  and extra challenges and even  collectibles the game also introduced  ultra beasts who would emerge from an  ultra wormhole you could also travel  into the wormhole to ultra space to find  legendary pokemon from older games like  mewtwo  2018 saw the first mainline pokemon  release on nintendo switch with let's go  eevee and pikachu which were remakes of  pokemon yellow but now not only were  they in full color they were 3d and the  control scheme was much easier to use in  fact you only needed one joy-con or the  pokeball plus accessory taking  inspiration from the wildly popular  pokemon mobile game pokemon go let's go  let you use motion controls to aim and  throw pokeballs to catch n